    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1010">

                <pb facs="1170" n="974" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg974"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of the Army Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1010<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United States
                        Fleet, and Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >King</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Navy Department</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1010-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">routine</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-26">26 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 358. CominCh sends serial 25 to CominCh
                    and CNO Admin for action. Action ad[dress]ee pass for info to ComNavEu and
                    ComNavForGermany.</p>
                <pb facs="1171" n="975" xml:id="pg975"/>
                <p>In consultation with Commodore Moran select officer qualified to sit on <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Capcraft</hi> Commission to select tugs suitable for
                    United States purposes. Have selected officer report to ComNavEu for temporary
                    duty on <hi rendition="#small-caps">Capcraft</hi> Commission.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1010-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1010-f1-content">
                <p>This message resulted from an agreement reached in Anglo-American conversations
                    at Babelsberg. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg299">p.
                        299</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
